# Rust / Cargo build output
/target
**/*.rs.bk

# Our own build artifacts (objects, linked kernel, ISO, isofiles staging)
/build

# Kernel image staged into the web tutorial (produced by `make web`)
/web/kernel.bin
# Optional self-hosted v86 assets (see web/README.md)
/web/libv86.js
/web/v86.wasm
/web/*.bin
# Staged for the browser tutorial by `make web` (reproducible; not committed)
/web/ziran.iso
# qemu-wasm live-boot assets (built by web/build-qemu-wasm.sh, ~60 MB — not committed).
# Emscripten keeps the qemu-system-x86_64.* names (baked into out.js); out.js/load.js
# are the renamed glue + FS loader.
/web/out.js
/web/load.js
/web/qemu-system-x86_64.*
/web/vendor/

# Tier-2 CTF exploit recipe (kept out of the public repo so the live challenge
# isn't pre-solved for a reader/scraper; the *concept* stays public, the concrete
# per-session recipe does not). Author's private operational note.
/ctf-server/*.private.md

